    },
    "body": "In `test/functional/interface_http.py`, I replaced `assert` with `assert_greater_than()` and\r\n`assert_greater_than_or_equal()` to make debugging easier on failure by printing both values being compared, instead of the previously set custom message.\r\n\r\nAsserts that have their custom message explaining the throttling failure being tested were left unchanged, as the helpers do not accept a message.\r\n\r\nSuggested in review of #36324:\r\nhttps://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36324#discussion_r4102111525\r\n\r\nI ran `build/test/functional/interface_http.py` before and after making the changes and it passed both times\r\n",
